    "justification": "The shifted critical-cone expansion is the correct local graph when moment noise and predictor queries move active faces at the same root-\\(n\\) scale.",
    "gap": "Geyer1994ConstrainedM and FangSantos2019Directional analyze a fixed constraint map; this result must keep the root-\\(n\\) movement of the query and the KKT slack jointly and uniformly over a compact direction set.",
    "consumer": "The local curve is the input needed to calibrate face-aware simultaneous bands rather than a pointwise fixed-cone approximation.",
    "proof_tex": "Put \\(\\epsilon=n^{-1/2}\\), \\(H_{n,u,t}=H_{\\theta_n(u)}(v_n(t))\\), and define \\(f_{n,u,t}\\) analogously. Twice continuous differentiability in the local chart, compactness, and legality of \\(v_n(t)\\) uniformly for large \\(n\\) give\n\\[\nH_{n,u,t}=H_0+\\epsilon\\dot H(u,t)+O(\\epsilon^2),\\qquad\nf_{n,u,t}=f_0+\\epsilon\\dot f(u,t)+O(\\epsilon^2).\n\\]\nThe ridge variational inequality first gives \\(\\sup_{u,t}\\|w_{n,u,t}-w_0\\|=O(\\epsilon)\\). A coordinate with \\(w_{0j}>0\\) remains positive. If \\(w_{0j}=0<s_{0j}\\), continuity of the multiplier keeps its slack positive, so complementarity makes \\(w_{n,u,t,j}=0\\). Remaining zero coordinates have \\(s_{0j}=0\\) and retain nonnegativity. Thus, for \\(w=w_0+\\epsilon k\\), bounded feasible \\(k\\)'s reduce to \\(\\mathcal C_0\\).\n\nSubtract the objective at \\(w_0\\), divide by \\(\\epsilon^2\\), and use \\(H_0w_0-f_0=-\\eta_0\\mathbf1+s_0\\). Equality makes the multiplier term vanish and positive-slack coordinates are fixed at zero. Uniformly on bounded \\(k,u,t\\), the criterion is\n\\[\n\\frac12k^\\prime H_0k+Q(u,t)^\\prime k+O(\\epsilon)(1+\\|k\\|^2).\n\\]\nBoth it and its limit are \\(2\\rho\\)-strongly convex. Subtracting variational inequalities shows their minimizers differ by \\(O(\\epsilon)\\), uniformly. Hence\n\\[\nw_{P_{\\theta_n(u)}}(v_n(t))=w_0+\\epsilon h(u,t)+O(\\epsilon^2).\n\\]\nThis includes any number of weak zero weights.\n\nLet \\(\\gamma_0=A_0^+a_{0,0}\\). Differentiating \\(A\\gamma=a_0\\) gives \\(A_0\\dot\\gamma=\\dot a_0-\\dot A\\gamma_0\\). Since \\(d_0\\in\\operatorname{row}(A_0)\\),\n\\[\n\\dot c(u)=\\dot d(u)^\\prime\\gamma_0+d_0^\\prime A_0^+\\{\\dot a_0(u)-\\dot A(u)\\gamma_0\\}.\n\\]\nTaylor expansion of risk gives, uniformly,\n\\[\n\\begin{split}\n\\sqrt n\\{R_{P_{\\theta_n(u)}}(v_n(t))-R_{P_{\\theta_0}}(v_0)\\}\n&=2b_0\\{\\dot c(u)-\\dot d(u)^\\prime w_0\\}+e_0^\\prime\\dot\\Sigma(u)e_0\\\\\n&\\quad+\\{-2b_0d_0-2\\Sigma_{D0}+2\\Sigma_{DD}w_0\\}^\\prime h(u,t)+o(1)\\\\\n&=a(u)+g^\\prime h(u,t)+o(1).\n\\end{split}\n\\]\nThis displays all completion, donor-mean, covariance, and weight terms.\n\nThe cone \\(\\mathcal C_0\\) is polyhedral, \\(H_0\\) is fixed positive definite, and \\(Q\\) is linear. Enumerating binding weak inequalities gives finitely many linear formulas with polyhedral feasibility regions. Uniqueness makes them agree on common boundaries, so \\(h\\) and \\(\\Psi_{\\theta_0}\\) are continuous piecewise affine. The variational inequality also gives\n\\[\n\\|h(u,t)-h(u',t')\\|\\leq(2\\rho)^{-1}\\|Q(u,t)-Q(u',t')\\|,\n\\]\nproving uniform continuity.",
